{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/148021-hunters-are-nutcases","id":148021,"title":"Hunters are nutcases.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-24T12:23:40-07:00","id":148021,"title":"Hunters are nutcases.","content":"I got stuck in traffic today, and I happen to be reading <i>Hunter-book: Martyr</i>, so I figured, &quot;Why not think about it?&quot; Especially since, as anyone who's read it knows, Joan is a complete nutcase. But then I got to thinking - really, all hunters are.<br /> <br /> A decade or two ago (I don't remember exactly) there was a story in Illinois, where I lived at the time, that some guy was arrested for parking on the side of the road and killing his kid(s -I don't remember how many he had), and when the cops arrested him, he said God had told him to do it. That sounds almost exactly like a pretty large percentage of hunters out there in the world. In particular, there's a guy in that book who considers killing his kid because he may have been turned into a vampire (apologies if you consider that a spoiler... given the nature of the books, it really shouldn't be). His excuse, if he gave it, would probably be something like, &quot;he was a monster,&quot; which sounds a lot like &quot;God told me to do it,&quot; to me. And there are hunters who would probably use those exact words, too (Joan comes to mind, and so does Crusader).<br /> <br /> So the question becomes, how does a hunter know the difference between &quot;He was wrong because I'm schizophrenic&quot; and &quot;He was wrong because the Messengers told me so&quot;? Waywards don't seem to be able to make that distinction in some cases, and some other Extremists suffer the same problem. And what if two guys get together and both say, &quot;I killed my kid because he was a demon.&quot; One of them is a hunter, but the other's just insane. There's no real way for the hunter to determine that the other man isn't a hunter, so ... what happens? Or does he find out he's working with a (worse) nut job when they find themselves in the presence of a real monster?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/426-big-brother","name":"Big Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar426_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T17:28:17-07:00","id":148277,"title":"","content":"thats..personally one of the horror elements of Hunter the reckoning, not knowing <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T23:13:06-07:00","id":148426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/148021-hunters-are-nutcases?p=148277#post148277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">thats..personally one of the horror elements of Hunter the reckoning, not knowing <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's plenty enough &quot;you just don't know&quot; just in being out of the loop on who's empowering you and why, or what you're capable of. We don't need to turn <i>They Live</i> with things that go bump in the night into <i>Frailty</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T00:26:21-07:00","id":148480,"title":"","content":"It is very interesting that Slashers in NWoD manifest supernatural powers related to their insanities.<br /> <br /> In CWoD, there may not be such a thing like Messengers at all and Hunters are just a kind of Slashers. Well, in NWoD many hunters who lose their shit end up as Slashers.<br /> <br /> But, I retcon the shit out of Reckoning anyway, and convert Hunter: The Vigil for CWoD, along with Slasher syndrome.<br /> <br /> Interesingly, one of proposed origins for Slashers is that Nimrod was the first Slasher (who made look Cain, the first murderer, nothing impressive). and Slasher syndrome spread as the curse of God along with new languages. And Nimrod did see angels/demons/whatever while going batshit insane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":2918,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","user":"Kat","date":". 05-25-2014, 03:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T05:20:26-07:00","id":148616,"title":"","content":"That's some pretty mean propaganda against the guy who built the first skyscraper. The story of Nimrod is another one of those biblical stories about how man needs to know his place and not challenge God. (like the whole apple from the tree of knowledge)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T05:30:17-07:00","id":148630,"title":"","content":"Nimrod cracked mentally from his lifetime of slaying supernaturals (of unknown identity) even before building the Tower. The Tower was not meant to challenge the God per se, but give excuse to kill off people. Abram slain Nimrod, but because WoD God is petty, he cursed remaining workers, traumatized and scared shitless by their boss, for refusing to believe Nimrod got shanked. The result as in Bible, with happy bonus of spreading Slasher phenomenon to humanity in general.<br /> <br /> But fitting NWoD, it is only one of myriad possible origins. Though the fact that a legendary Hunter became the First Slasher fits the fact that some Hunters in Vigil crack mentally and become Slashers.<br /> <br /> I want to integrate Slasher into CWoD, but I'm not set yet on their origin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T06:13:12-07:00","id":148642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Big Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/148021-hunters-are-nutcases#post148021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the question becomes, how does a hunter know the difference between &quot;He was wrong because I'm schizophrenic&quot; and &quot;He was wrong because the Messengers told me so&quot;? <b>Waywards don't seem to be able to make that distinction in some cases</b>, and some other Extremists suffer the same problem. And what if two guys get together and both say, &quot;I killed my kid because he was a demon.&quot; One of them is a hunter, but the other's just insane. There's no real way for the hunter to determine that the other man isn't a hunter, so ... what happens? Or does he find out he's working with a (worse) nut job when they find themselves in the presence of a real monster?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm. I've always thought that Waywards were some of the best in making those distinctions. They're able to separate the &quot;good&quot; from the &quot;bad&quot; and are able to kill without conscience regardless of a monster's plea. A martyr will be sympathetic...which is why in the Martyr Hunter book he is even questioning the option of sparing the kid.<br /> <br /> A Wayward would kill the kid, and any other people in the vicinity if that's what it took to get the job done.<br /> <br /> Remember, Reckoning Hunters are just waking up to a world gone insane and the endgame near. They're going out to hunt, with some powers but still human mind you, and hunting some of the worst things the human eye can see. They're slightly more prepared than normal hunters(from HH/HH2) because of their powers, but in the end, it's still a fools' errand. They're all going to be a little &quot;off.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T08:24:04-07:00","id":148710,"title":"","content":"Well, not getting into nWoD, since it doesn't have anything to do with what I was talking about, and I don't know much about it anyway...<br /> <br /> DoL, you're right I guess. They can make the distinction, they just sorta... don't. Whereas most of the others have the potential to care about us &quot;norms,&quot; Waywards figure we just get in the way of the conflict. If they kill a few hundred children, oh well - at least they got that rot. There will always be more kids. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/426-big-brother","name":"Big Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar426_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T22:45:35-07:00","id":149159,"title":"","content":"Of course their nuts one and all, after all they are supernatural beings that think they are normal humans despite being able to turn anything in their hands into a Flaming Weapon of Doom(tm). Cause you know all humans can, right? Except that guy who is totally supernatural because he can summon fire to form a fiery weapon of doom and the voices in my head agree that he should be killed...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T01:49:46-07:00","id":149222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> after all they are supernatural beings that think they are normal humans despite being able to turn anything in their hands into a Flaming Weapon of Doom(tm). </div> </div> </div>One of many reasons why Vigil is superior. Hunters are mortals. Even Slashers are mortals, though in the scourge territory the line between mortal and supernatural starts blurring especially when it comes to Masks and Mutants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T05:29:12-07:00","id":149324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/148021-hunters-are-nutcases?p=149222#post149222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One of many reasons why Vigil is superior. Hunters are mortals. Even Slashers are mortals, though in the scourge territory the line between mortal and supernatural starts blurring especially when it comes to Masks and Mutants.</div> </div> </div> </div>And it works because Vampires in that setting start off slightly weaker than random passers-by. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/919-harlokin","name":"harlokin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T06:28:09-07:00","id":149343,"title":"","content":"Seriously, Hunters Hunted 2's hunters don't need Numina to hunt.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I disregard Reckoning and use Vigil in CWoD.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T06:56:28-07:00","id":149378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/148021-hunters-are-nutcases?p=149222#post149222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>One of many reasons why Vigil is superior.</b> Hunters are mortals. Even Slashers are mortals, though in the scourge territory the line between mortal and supernatural starts blurring especially when it comes to Masks and Mutants.</div> </div> </div> </div>Psh. Blasphemy. They're both good in their own right.<br /> <br /> And hunters from Reckoning are human. They're simply super powered ones. Captain America is still a human. Iron Fist is still human. A bullet in the head(or chest) will kill a Reckoning hunter just as it would a Vigil one. And just how it wouldn't kill a vampire or mummy. <br /> <br /> Reckoning hunters simply have better offensive and defensive capabilities to even the playing field. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T07:06:09-07:00","id":149379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Psh. Blasphemy. They're both good in their own right. </div> </div> </div>My resident Tech Priest and Vigil GM of course disagrees. <br /> <br /> Advanced Armory of Task Force: VALKYRIE &gt; Edges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T10:06:24-07:00","id":149465,"title":"","content":"... but again, we're not talking nWoD here.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, DoL, technically a bullet to the head would kill a mummy, it just wouldn't be a very long-lasting death. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/426-big-brother","name":"Big Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar426_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T10:24:50-07:00","id":149497,"title":"","content":"I guess I'll make seperate thread to not clog this thread with Slasher talk. As my friend helped me give explanation for Slashers in CWoD, though it alters the backstory of Caine in one subtle aspect (No, he is not the first Slasher).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T12:05:14-07:00","id":149612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/148021-hunters-are-nutcases?p=149343#post149343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously, Hunters Hunted 2's hunters don't need Numina to hunt.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I disregard Reckoning and use Vigil in CWoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>When Hunter first came out, I had a readthrough of a friend's borrowed corebook and none of it was how I had pictured the Hunters of the WoD to be. This made it really hard for me to get into Hunter and really annoyed at the things I felt were seriously cheesy and yeah, the system seems to be full of nutjobs. Along comes New WoD and when I'm complaining (yes, Bitching too) with a gamer friend about how I had always pictured Hunter: the Reckoning being, he informed me that everything I had ranted about en tangent for about an hour, was what Hunter: the Vigil was all about... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I completely agree on dumping Reckoning and using Vigil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T16:48:01-07:00","id":149808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darling_Rose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/148021-hunters-are-nutcases?p=149612#post149612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When Hunter first came out, I had a readthrough of a friend's borrowed corebook and none of it was how I had pictured the Hunters of the WoD to be. This made it really hard for me to get into Hunter and really annoyed at the things I felt were seriously cheesy and yeah, the system seems to be full of nutjobs. Along comes New WoD and when I'm complaining (yes, Bitching too) with a gamer friend about how I had always pictured Hunter: the Reckoning being, he informed me that everything I had ranted about en tangent for about an hour, was what Hunter: the Vigil was all about... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I completely agree on dumping Reckoning and using Vigil.</div> </div> </div> </div>WW already had several years worth of &quot;mortals that hunt monsters&quot; prior to 1999. They pretty much had to do something starkly different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T17:08:54-07:00","id":149829,"title":"","content":"Meh, they could upgrade Hunters Hunted 2 and Project Twilight into full splat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T17:54:39-07:00","id":149875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/148021-hunters-are-nutcases?p=149829#post149829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meh, they could upgrade Hunters Hunted 2 and Project Twilight into full splat.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why? The focus for full splats was on monsters (whether the individuals wanted to admit it to themselves or not, such as with Mages). The Imbued are basically anti-monsters, sharing a great deal of conceptual space but largely opposed to the other full splats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T22:02:44-07:00","id":150033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/148021-hunters-are-nutcases?p=149829#post149829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meh, they could upgrade Hunters Hunted 2 and Project Twilight into full splat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I liked how Vigil approached the hunter orgs, a book full of them instead of one made from whole cloth.<br /> <br /> And then Hunters Hunted 2 got its strech goals, the book is really as close to Vigil style as we can get.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T22:26:11-07:00","id":150040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/148021-hunters-are-nutcases?p=149829#post149829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meh, they could upgrade Hunters Hunted 2 and Project Twilight into full splat.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is what I originally expected Hunter the Reckoning to be. Obviously it wasn't which it has the dubious honor of being the only WoD product I have ever sold away at the first opportunity. Bottom line, it was advertised as being a game about mortals realizing there are supernatural beings about and doing something about it but the game itself was about self deluded supernatural beings attacking other supernatural beings. Not at all what I had expected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T23:05:33-07:00","id":150060,"title":"","content":"I think that for Imbued, the distinction is purely academic. What ultimately matters is the lengths some Imbued will go to in order to get the job done, and whether those lengths are tolerable by other hunters (for whatever end). A Redeemer may turn on a Wayward for being worse than the monsters they would kill due to collateral, just as a Wayward may turn on a Redeemer for collaboration.<br /> <br /> Case in point, the last HtR game session in a chronicle we (sporadically) play. This wraith somehow ended up with our group as fetters, and was threatening to harm bystanders unless we acted out this goofy-ass little passion play. The wraith let slip we were its fetters, so my Martyr immediately put his gun to his own head. Cue pants-shitting on both sides of the encounter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T00:11:05-07:00","id":150084,"title":"","content":"I don't know I always felt that Hunters that are &quot;just humans&quot; lkke they were in huntets hunted are much more frightening than the Hunters from Reckoning. I mean yeah wow... you're a powerfull supernatural being with the only mission to destroy supernatural beings. THATS THE TECHNOCRACY'S ROLE DAMN! And hunters were never as cool as the MIB cause MIBs are our first, strongest and only line of defense, AND they dress in Black <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The huntershunted-hunters on the other hand are freaking me out. I mean they got (almost) no supernatural powers and manage to hunt down vampire-elders, werewolfs and other shit just because they prepare perfectly and have a impressive improvisation-talent. I some kinda feel that a &quot;really&quot; good hunter could be jarod from &quot;the pretender&quot; series.<br /> Those guys scare elders out because they maanage to do things they are not supposed to be able to do.<br /> <br /> anyone feels the same? Or maybe at least sees my point? (Not a native speaker so I hope my post makes any sense as I wrote it)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1235-eadee","name":"Eadee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T02:59:02-07:00","id":150157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The huntershunted-hunters on the other hand are freaking me out. I mean they got (almost) no supernatural powers and manage to hunt down vampire-elders, werewolfs and other shit just because they prepare perfectly and have a impressive improvisation-talent. I some kinda feel that a &quot;really&quot; good hunter could be jarod from &quot;the pretender&quot; series.<br /> Those guys scare elders out because they maanage to do things they are not supposed to be able to do. </div> </div> </div>Note that even with preparation they can sustain some heavy losses. Akritai took out Triphosa, 4th or 5th Gen Malkavian Methusaleh. At cost of half its personel. <br /> <br /> It's not that weird given the fact concerted efforts of humanity could wipe off vampires from the face of Earth (at least majority of the species), hence Masquerade. And elders are not such unstoppable killing machines since they have weaknesses against thing like fire unless they have Fortitude. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T06:10:59-07:00","id":150229,"title":"","content":"We've all become God's madmen, all of us. <br /> - Van Helsing, Bram Stoker's Dracula","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3078-coffee-zombie","name":"Coffee Zombie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T09:23:05-07:00","id":150426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eadee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/148021-hunters-are-nutcases?p=150084#post150084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know I always felt that Hunters that are &quot;just humans&quot; lkke they were in huntets hunted are much more frightening than the Hunters from Reckoning. I mean yeah wow... you're a powerfull supernatural being with the only mission to destroy supernatural beings. THATS THE TECHNOCRACY'S ROLE DAMN!<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>There's a difference between trimming the excesses and wholesale extermination. Most of the Imbued tend to fall under the former category. The Technocracy tends to fall overwhelmingly into the latter, since it labels everyone a Reality Deviant and the party line that hard men making hard decision hold everyone to is to kill, kill, and kill some more. Anyone who doesn't think that all you need is kill gets reprogrammed or snuffed out. While some Imbued do take things that far, the members of the Mercy Creeds can be counted on to not do that, and they make up a significant portion of Imbued - certainly more than the Waywards. They also are regular people in the sense that they're trying to hold down jobs and don't have hidden doom fortresses and the support of societal influence at every level, that kind of thing. The Technocracy is a vast distance from that, being monsters that warp reality to try and make it fit their incomplete vision of safety uber alles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T12:14:37-07:00","id":150695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eadee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/148021-hunters-are-nutcases?p=150084#post150084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know I always felt that Hunters that are &quot;just humans&quot; lkke they were in huntets hunted are much more frightening than the Hunters from Reckoning. I mean yeah wow... <b>you're a powerfull supernatural being with the only mission to destroy supernatural beings.</b> THATS THE TECHNOCRACY'S ROLE DAMN! And hunters were never as cool as the MIB cause MIBs are our first, strongest and only line of defense, AND they dress in Black <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No. Not true. Martyrs, Redeemers, Innocents, etc. missions can be far, far different than this. Saur Ops Specialist stated it far better than I could. Still, as someone that loves Reckoning, I'm almost sad to see it being viewed by so many as unwanted, unnecessary, and in some cases, not being played to it's fullest potential. All the hunter books in both CWOD(Reckoning, HH, HH2, Arcanum, Project Twilight, etc.), and NWOD(Vigil) are amazing in their own right. Filled with the potential to have awesome games that have brought me immense joy. Guess I've just had good storytellers that have brought out the best in each of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T13:11:03-07:00","id":150744,"title":"","content":"If I want to play a human with gonzo powers, I play Mage. And there are Mage hunters as displayed in one Storyteller Guides with example of Sons of Ether hunter tracking a vampire. <br /> <br /> Hunter is not race, it's vocation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T13:24:52-07:00","id":150757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/148021-hunters-are-nutcases?p=150744#post150744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I want to play a human with gonzo powers, I play Mage. And there are Mage hunters as displayed in one Storyteller Guides with example of Sons of Ether hunter tracking a vampire.<br /> <br /> Hunter is not race, it's vocation.</div> </div> </div> </div>This here is why I am don't like the Imbued. In the previous hunter books, you could have werewolves raised by Society of Leopold, Hunters Hunted 1 had the first ever named werewolf npc,etc. Hunters are people who take up arms for different reasons, no matter what the specie.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T13:28:22-07:00","id":150758,"title":"","content":"@saur &amp; dude: okay maybe Hunter:tR is a better game than I believe. But if what you say is true and its not revolving around hunters killing supernatural beings. Then it kinda misses the point from what I expect of a game named Hunter:tR.<br /> <br /> Maybe I would've liked it if it was called &quot;Dudes with powers: the karmic resolution&quot;. But I saw H:tR as a failed try to make hunters more dangerous and &quot;kewl&quot; at least the Title implied somehow it deals with Hunters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1235,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1235-eadee","user":"Eadee","date":". 05-27-2014, 05:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1235-eadee","name":"Eadee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T20:05:59-07:00","id":150964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eadee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/148021-hunters-are-nutcases?p=150758#post150758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@saur &amp; dude: okay maybe Hunter:tR is a better game than I believe. But if what you say is true and its not revolving around hunters killing supernatural beings. Then it kinda misses the point from what I expect of a game named Hunter:tR.<br /> <br /> Maybe I would've liked it if it was called &quot;Dudes with powers: the karmic resolution&quot;. But I saw H:tR as a failed try to make hunters more dangerous and &quot;kewl&quot; at least the Title implied somehow it deals with Hunters.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It's all good. To each his/her own. I'm not trying to sell anyone on Reckoning. I couldn't care less. I love it. Just like I love Vigil. And just like I love HH2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T12:21:42-07:00","id":151581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/148021-hunters-are-nutcases?p=150744#post150744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I want to play a human with gonzo powers, I play Mage. And there are Mage hunters as displayed in one Storyteller Guides with example of Sons of Ether hunter tracking a vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which only works if you like/tolerate/begrudgingly don't hate Mage. Some of us very much despise it utterly. Besides, &quot;clueless people thrown into the deep end&quot; only really describes a minority of Mages.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hunter is not race, it's vocation. </div> </div> </div>Then how do you account for your great love of slashers from the nWoD?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T14:57:44-07:00","id":151739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Then how do you account for your great love of slashers from the nWoD</span><br /> </span><br /> </div> </div> </div>While some hunters crack and end up as Slashers, note that many more Slashers never took up the Vigil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T17:56:56-07:00","id":151874,"title":"","content":"ok....in hunter, madness is a tool. it helps hunters not to have the need for them to use any focus. What is the price? madness itself.<br /> Second: the whole mages being the saveurs of mindkind is bullshit, a mage is not a hero. a mage is far from being a hero. mages are selfish guys and girls who cant accept the rules of reality so they create a new reality, not caring on the human kind. thats the horror element of mage, the fact that we humans are utterly fucked up against a guy who can make you breath cheese and turn your heart into candy if he is bored.<br /> <br /> Spoilers incoming:<br /> <br /> No one knows How do hunters were born, theres stories in the storytellers book..but officially , theres ONE hunter who might have an idea (violin99) but even though, he is not sure.<br /> <br /> Its belived that Imbueds are the last line of defense of humanity against the darkness, the tool to STOP ARMAGEDON/APOCALYPSE/GEHENNA/JIHAD/THE WINTER/MY MOM from ever happening.<br /> They were imbued with powers based on psycological steriotypes of people in the middle of some sort of crisis.<br /> <br /> Whats the catch of hunter..Why it is a reckoning?<br /> <br /> Hunters are born on the end of days. The darkness is wining.<br /> Demons Roam the earth creating new eldritch horrors<br /> Lycans are involved with attacks against industries and slowly staling new technology<br /> Wizards are turning the wheel of what is reality, forcing their madness upon the consensus and using humans as playthings<br /> Faeries are living nightmares, feeding of the dreams and leaving humans as an empty shell<br /> Ghosts roam the earth, making people be aware that theres worsts things than death.<br /> and vampires control societies, forcing secret wars and killing hundreds or thousands as collateral damage.<br /> Humanity Cant Fight anymore.<br /> <br /> We had our chances to strike this threat on one single blow, we had the inquisition and we failed. humans keep trying to stay away from all this and now they are winning. The armageddon is coming, and after many years of abuse against humans. Something said &quot;No More.&quot; and decided to give the tools to mindkind to fight one last time. to push the doomsday clock's handles as far as we could.<br /> <br /> Why is hunter not only about killing supernaturals?<br /> This is part of the metaplot so, be warned. Theres 7 Creeds, each one representing the state of mind of the hunter when he faced the supernatural and determinating his powers. this are devided in 3 tiers based on the base of their beliefs. This ones are<br /> Avenger. : Not only the one who fights for revenge, but the one who was stepped on his entire life and said &quot;No more. &quot; he who is fueled by rage and a need for social justice or justice in general.<br /> Defender. : The Shield, the protector, he who takes care of protecting the flock from the darkness.<br /> Judge. : The leader, the politic, the strategic mind, he who judges and drops the hammer upon thy. Guilty or Innocent, no one can pass his judgment.<br /> Visionary: The long term strategy, the ones who investigate, who think, who wish to create a better tomorrow and think forward.<br /> Martyrdoom.: He who takes the pain for the cause, who makes personal sacrifices to guide the group to victory.<br /> Redemeer.: Not all monsters have to be inhuman, these are who look for the humanity within the beast, the ones who wish to find a cure for their condition. the ones who wish to save the darkness from itself<br /> Innocent.: Why?. thats all...curiosity, intellect. Not naivity, but rather curiosity. those who are willing to Understand the mind of a monster and wish to know simply: Why.<br /> <br /> <br /> Depending on the creed, the game might take a different point of view. from hunting only, to find a cure, to find salvation, to prepare mindkind for the day after the storm.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T18:15:32-07:00","id":151886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/148021-hunters-are-nutcases?p=151739#post151739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While some hunters crack and end up as Slashers, note that many more Slashers never took up the Vigil.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't actually argue against my point. Quite the opposite, really, since they just end up getting dunked into being hunters of a sort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T02:26:42-07:00","id":152277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That doesn't actually argue against my point. Quite the opposite, really, since they just end up getting dunked into being hunters of a sort. </div> </div> </div>No, they are not meant to be played as player characters, but antagonists. If your GM runs chronicle with Slashers, it's more probably you will play hunters dealing with serial killer sprees. Hunters becoming Slashers after slipping to 0 Morality is optional. Some Slashers do target supernaturals, but it does not have to do anything with upholding the Vigil, they are just serial killers with specific target.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T04:28:54-07:00","id":152351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/148021-hunters-are-nutcases?p=151874#post151874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ok....in hunter, madness is a tool. it helps hunters not to have the need for them to use any focus. What is the price? madness itself. Second: the whole mages being the saveurs of mindkind is bullshit, a mage is not a hero. a mage is far from being a hero. mages are selfish guys and girls who cant accept the rules of reality so they create a new reality, not caring on the human kind. thats the horror element of mage, the fact that we humans are utterly fucked up against a guy who can make you breath cheese and turn your heart into candy if he is bored.</div> </div> </div> </div> And this is why I can't work with Hunter unless it's a stand alone game. It runs with a completely flipped set of stereotypes. This universe does not play well with others. You can't have any sort of Hunter crossing over into any game without the Hunter coming off as a raging persecuting warmonger the likes of which even skinheads would think is taking things too seriously. The game diverges to the point that it isn't about the different views or having a higher ideal for Humanity, it becomes all about the US vs THEM. So yeah... They all look like nut jobs outside of their game universe and often, even within it. They like to think of themselves like they're agents of S.H.I.E.L.D, but really appear more like human race supremacists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T04:31:18-07:00","id":152353,"title":"","content":"All that being said.... I really liked this Hunter: the Reckoning vid. I would totally watch this movie. <a href=\"http://youtu.be/ASxr8M5yvCE\" target=\"_blank\">http://youtu.be/ASxr8M5yvCE</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T06:45:24-07:00","id":152457,"title":"","content":"I don't think mages are detached from humanity though. Humans have in them drive to change what's around (unless completely apathetic), it's just that mages know better how to tamper with reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T07:00:05-07:00","id":152468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darling_Rose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/148021-hunters-are-nutcases?p=152351#post152351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And this is why I can't work with Hunter unless it's a stand alone game. It runs with a completely flipped set of stereotypes. This universe does not play well with others. You can't have any sort of Hunter crossing over into any game without the Hunter coming off as a raging persecuting warmonger the likes of which even skinheads would think is taking things too seriously. The game diverges to the point that it isn't about the different views or having a higher ideal for Humanity, it becomes all about the US vs THEM. So yeah... They all look like nut jobs outside of their game universe and often, even within it. They like to think of themselves like they're agents of S.H.I.E.L.D, but really appear more like human race supremacists.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well said.<br /> <br /> By itself, Hunter might be a good game. As part of any sort of mixed WoD universe, it makes no sense and adds nothing new thematically or morally to the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T11:23:32-07:00","id":152723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darling_Rose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/148021-hunters-are-nutcases?p=152351#post152351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And this is why I can't work with Hunter unless it's a stand alone game. It runs with a completely flipped set of stereotypes. This universe does not play well with others. <b>You can't have any sort of Hunter crossing over into any game without the Hunter coming off as a raging persecuting warmonger the likes of which even skinheads would think is taking things too seriously.</b> The game diverges to the point that it isn't about the different views or having a higher ideal for Humanity, it becomes all about the US vs THEM. So yeah... They all look like nut jobs outside of their game universe and often, even within it. They like to think of themselves like they're agents of S.H.I.E.L.D, but really appear more like human race supremacists.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is totally untrue. But considering I've seen it posted by others at least two times now so I'm guessing people are simply ignoring posts that explain otherwise.<br /> <br /> <br /> You CAN have hunters(from Reckoning) that can cross into ANY game and have them work together with various supernaturals. It can be done. Quite easily as long as the storyteller knows what they're doing. I've seen it done with Redeemers, especially.<br /> <br /> Are you going to have an Avenger working together with a vampire? Unlikely. But again, it can be done. And I'm not even going to bother touching the skinhead comment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":95,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","user":"Fat Larry","date":". 05-29-2014, 03:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T12:17:30-07:00","id":154084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/148021-hunters-are-nutcases?p=152723#post152723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> You CAN have hunters(from Reckoning) that can cross into ANY game and have them work together with various supernaturals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. There are also examples in the various splatbooks of certain Hunters being on at least speaking terms with supernaturals. Bookworm 55 gets a bit closer than that when he is dating a vampire. Not all Imbued are rageing lunatics. Although some certainly are. That is, in my opinion one of the appeals of HtR, the characters are a motley selection of humanity, chosen apparently at random, from all walks of life, and told by a voice they can't ignore; &quot;The Monsters are real.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1441-ersatz","name":"Ersatz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T12:32:41-07:00","id":154098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/148021-hunters-are-nutcases?p=152457#post152457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think mages are detached from humanity though. Humans have in them drive to change what's around (unless completely apathetic), it's just that mages know better how to tamper with reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personal opinions don't really enter into it. Mages are in contact with an Avatar, which is a shard of something distinctly outside the bounds of reality. It changes them so that they are no longer affected by the Delirium regardless of how high or low their nerves are, and plays tricks with existence. If someone expresses discontent with the force of gravity or the flow of time, that's normal. If someone sets out to defy it, it's a fool's errand, a vain and impossible hope.<br /> <br /> If someone sets out to break the world and does it... that's horrifying. And the beings comfortable with this prospect? They're not even of this world any more, much less human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T12:52:29-07:00","id":154118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/148021-hunters-are-nutcases?p=154098#post154098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If someone sets out to break the world and does it... that's horrifying. And the beings comfortable with this prospect? They're not even of this world any more, much less human.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The ability to set a tire iron on fire with your mind also breaks the world. It is horrifying (more than mages even, since it is not subject to paradox). Whoever it is that is able to do that is a monster, not even remotely human.<br /> <br /> <br /> Right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T13:08:24-07:00","id":154125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ersatz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/148021-hunters-are-nutcases?p=154084#post154084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. There are also examples in the various splatbooks of certain Hunters being on at least speaking terms with supernaturals. Bookworm 55 gets a bit closer than that when he is dating a vampire. Not all Imbued are rageing lunatics. Although some certainly are. That is, in my opinion one of the appeals of HtR, the characters are a motley selection of humanity, chosen apparently at random, from all walks of life, and told by a voice they can't ignore; &quot;The Monsters are real.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue that B55 is still pretty out of his mind, just in a different way. And he still hears voices. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> SixFootChicken has a point though, the ability to set a tire iron on fire isn't exactly insignificant, especially given that it's not subject to paradox. That said, I'm not sure that it gives them the right to start offling people just because the voices in their head tells 'em to. And then there are the people without really obvious powers... Would you really believe someone who used Discern and decided to kill someone based on that, a voice in his head, and maybe some &quot;Second Sight&quot;?<br /> <br /> <i>Edit: And damnit, I just have to say it: &quot;The ability to set a tire iron on fire with your mind is insignificant next to the power of the Force.&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/426-big-brother","name":"Big Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar426_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T13:13:12-07:00","id":154132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SixFootChicken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/148021-hunters-are-nutcases?p=154118#post154118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The ability to set a tire iron on fire with your mind also breaks the world. It is horrifying (more than mages even, since it is not subject to paradox). Whoever it is that is able to do that is a monster, not even remotely human.<br /> <br /> <br /> Right?</div> </div> </div> </div>We've already covered that the Imbued are anti-monsters. They've been tapped by some forces representing life and death to take some form of action relating to monsters. What makes them arguable more human than mages is that they're trying to preserve what's valuable to them and prevent the world from crashing down around them completely, which involves staying with the lives that they had rather than sitting in fortresses of solitude and working ancient rituals to some esoteric effect, or parking their butts in Horizon and forgetting about the world from which they came from a few centuries longer than they would have been otherwise able to live. In fact, they have only the most fleeting access to the spirit worlds, so they are completely incapable of fleeing the world of flesh and matter for another. This is far more significant than possibly being able to light up an object to hit someone (a point which the books waffle on constantly and which have been argued about more than a few times on the internet), because it keeps them grounded in the business they were occupied with before the Messengers chose them for another job. Hopefully, hindsight will endow the next iteration of H:TR with mechanics to encourage not abandoning everything and moving off the grid. Only one Creed really has an excuse to do that, and not all of them should, in spite of being blatantly labeled Hermits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T15:03:20-07:00","id":154205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/148021-hunters-are-nutcases?p=154132#post154132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> We've already covered that the Imbued are anti-monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div> Existentially, yeah, we've covered that. From outside perspective, if I were a normal human carrying a gun in america and I was confronted with a guy throwing cement bricks with his mind at another guy setting a tire-iron on fire I'd shoot them both. Monster or anti-monster their super powers present a threat to joe-blow. Good luck convincing a scared witness which one is supposed to be the good guy after seeing two normal looking people trying to kill each other with mutant powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T15:27:58-07:00","id":154224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darling_Rose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/148021-hunters-are-nutcases?p=154205#post154205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Existentially, yeah, we've covered that. From outside perspective, if I were a normal human carrying a gun in america and I was confronted with a guy throwing cement bricks with his mind at another guy setting a tire-iron on fire I'd shoot them both. Monster or anti-monster their super powers present a threat to joe-blow. Good luck convincing a scared witness which one is supposed to be the good guy after seeing two normal looking people trying to kill each other with mutant powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>The tire iron wouldn't appear to be on fire unless you were a monster, too. At least, that's how W20 weighs in on Cleave in the antagonists chapter. The H:TR core also mentions that normal people will Roll to Disbelieve and not notice, like someone faced with a Crinos werewolf rationalizing it away. Hence why one of the Imbued in the core fiction demonstrated his powers on camera, but no one ever thought it was anything but SFX and visual trickery, and only involved with make a chair suddenly fly apart at that (no one saw a flaming sword).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T19:01:51-07:00","id":154432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/148021-hunters-are-nutcases?p=149343#post149343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously, Hunters Hunted 2's hunters don't need Numina to hunt.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I disregard Reckoning and use Vigil in CWoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also agree with this (and the general sentiments expressed throughout this thread). For me, the basic premise of Hunter is normal humans taking back the night from monsters. It sort of becomes a broken Aesop if they have to use supernatural powers to do so, the issue of whether Imbued hunters are monsters totally aside. It also diminishes their role as underdogs who have to scrape by on mundane advantages like resourcefulness, teamwork, equipment, and all those other qualities that let us become the dominant species in a world with bigger nastier predators. Why does it need to be different with supernatural ones?<br /> <br /> Supernatural hunters aren't an inherently bad idea, but I preferred how Vigil made its Endowments an optional, morally iffy thing that characters could question, debate, and wring their hands over. You can make a huge case for the Cheiron Group in particular turning humans into monsters.<br /> <br /> And yeah, Hunters Hunted 2's hunters kick ass. I remember reading how one of the small-name organizations destroyed Tryphosa and just thinking &quot;holy crap, these guys killed a Methuselah. Normal humans are badass.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T20:16:52-07:00","id":154482,"title":"","content":"@Saur-Ops<br /> So in your opinion Mages are monstrous for being in contact with an Awakened Avatar, you do realize each and every human who has not been attack with soul destroying might (ie Gilgul, Embrace etc.) has at least a miniscule chance of awakening which means all of us are in contact with these things you label as powers from outside reality, but Hunters who are literally touched by these Supernatural Beings called Messengers who constantly whisper to them things like asking them to murder people around them because they are allegedly supernatural beings, with little to no other proof outside of that provided by these same Messengers through powers given by them. Still you believe you have a case for presenting Hunters as humans over Mages who literally are humans who have awakened the potential present within each human on the planet.<br /> <br /> Avatars are much more part of every human on the planet than the Messengers could ever hope to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T20:52:26-07:00","id":154499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/148021-hunters-are-nutcases?p=154482#post154482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Saur-Ops<br /> So in your opinion Mages are monstrous for being in contact with an Awakened Avatar, you do realize each and every human who has not been attack with soul destroying might (ie Gilgul, Embrace etc.) has at least a miniscule chance of awakening which means all of us are in contact with these things you label as powers from outside reality, but Hunters who are literally touched by these Supernatural Beings called Messengers who constantly whisper to them things like asking them to murder people around them because they are allegedly supernatural beings, with little to no other proof outside of that provided by these same Messengers through powers given by them. Still you believe you have a case for presenting Hunters as humans over Mages who literally are humans who have awakened the potential present within each human on the planet.<br /> <br /> Avatars are much more part of every human on the planet than the Messengers could ever hope to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>One could also say that you might well catch a transformative disease that only infects humans, drastically altering them into post-humans. Meanwhile, Imbued are only empowered if they invoke Conviction. Conviction is not invoked all the time - but an Avatar, and all the bits of being a mystic(k) are always with a Mage.<br /> <br /> Also, none of the Imbued are asked or commanded to murder. They get to see the truth, and they decide how to respond... or to not respond, even.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 05-30-2014, 11:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T07:12:54-07:00","id":154799,"title":"","content":"If the Embrace destroys the soul, what do vampires claim when they commit diablerie on each other?<br /> <br /> Anyhoo, Hunter the Reckoning's biggest problem (imho) is that it lacked enough variation or sustainability as a major gameline. It was perfect for something like Orpheus, which was a limited run. However, HtR has to deal with the fact that its only purpose is to act as a foil to the other lines. Even Mummy and Kindred of the East (which were supplement lines originally, as they required Vampire to run) had their own internal struggles that sustained their own purpose. Sure, they both dealt with Cainites, but they didn't <i>have </i>to. If a Hunter doesn't hunt the monsters, (s)he isn't a hunter. Hunters Hunted (either edition) was a supplement book that contained different kinds of Hunters, with differing abilities and origins. Demon Hunter X (while terrible) was also a proper supplement book which acted as a foil to its respective arena, and neither it nor Hunters Hunted required a complete game line with their own splat books beyond the core.<br /> <br /> HtR could have used Conviction as an additional means to fuel willpower, like True Faith, with the belief in oneself rather than a higher power (instead a higher purpose). Rather than a wonky resource for angel (or alien depending on mood) powers. The Sight could have been a complete constant (&quot;you cannot unsee the hidden world!&quot;) or a flicker that appeared when needed, or not, with an entirely unknown origin. Either could have better served the capacity for storytelling better than &quot;I spend my bloo... err, Conviction to activate my superpowers, do I see any weird shit?&quot; Now, I will admit the Messengers are an awesome fluff piece for the story. I just didn't (and still don't) think that HtR needed the hunters to be able to create force fields with their minds or summon flaming swords to fight monsters. Hell, just being immune to their control powers is a huge damn edge to fighting them anyone, as well as the ability to see through their illusions. Could have even extended the Angel innate abilities further (without Lore or Theurgy nonsense) that they have by giving them more, or even all, of the innate abilities from Demon the Fallen. The ability to pattern sense even if they don't understand what they are sensing is an awesome one.<br /> <br /> Oh, and yes... Vigil is better. That isn't even a subjective opinion. It clearly has more options, totally internal problems to deal with, doesn't require anything but the corebook (including the WoD one) to play properly, and it has the Lucifuge. Everything is better with the Lucifuge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1604-oliver-the-bold","name":"Oliver the Bold","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T09:16:47-07:00","id":154891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oliver the Bold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/148021-hunters-are-nutcases?p=154799#post154799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demon Hunter X (while terrible)</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry. I stopped reading here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T12:43:22-07:00","id":155105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/148021-hunters-are-nutcases?p=154891#post154891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry. I stopped reading here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Sure, the mechanics are solid and it works fine in the setting which it takes place (Wuxia Movie-Asia)... but can you truly tell me that it isn't patently ridiculous? I mean, the artwork in the book alone gets a laugh out of me every time I see it. It's like if you combined Hunter the Reckoning with a John Woo movie, and then added kung fu cyborgs. Its so silly, it doesn't take place in a World of Darkness, it takes place in a World of Cliches.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1604-oliver-the-bold","name":"Oliver the Bold","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T14:35:15-07:00","id":155222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oliver the Bold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/148021-hunters-are-nutcases?p=155105#post155105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? Sure, the mechanics are solid and it works fine in the setting which it takes place (Wuxia Movie-Asia)... but can you truly tell me that it isn't patently ridiculous? I mean, the artwork in the book alone gets a laugh out of me every time I see it. It's like if you combined Hunter the Reckoning with a John Woo movie, and then added kung fu cyborgs. Its so silly, it doesn't take place in a World of Darkness, it takes place in a World of Cliches.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh don't get me wrong. It's definitely silly. But I think it was supposed to be silly. Your view of it exactly why I loved it! I know a number of people that I have gamed with over the years also profess their love for it.<br /> <br /> This thread is a great example of how awesome White Wolf did with its game lines. There was plenty of material there for people to choose what they wanted to get out of a game. Some loved Hunter the Reckoning(like myself), others hated it. Some love Mage, others hate it. White Wolf was great at creating all these amazing worlds that touched people in different ways. I'm just glad Onyx Path is here to continue that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T17:50:20-07:00","id":155324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oliver the Bold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/148021-hunters-are-nutcases?p=155105#post155105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? Sure, the mechanics are solid and it works fine in the setting which it takes place (Wuxia Movie-Asia)... but can you truly tell me that it isn't patently ridiculous? I mean, the artwork in the book alone gets a laugh out of me every time I see it. It's like if you combined Hunter the Reckoning with a John Woo movie, and then added kung fu cyborgs. Its so silly, it doesn't take place in a World of Darkness, it takes place in a World of Cliches.</div> </div> </div> </div>In large part, it comes courtesy of Mage - quite literally, in fact. Yi the Archer was apparently a Mage (one version, anyway), and the equipment that SF0 uses is produced by the Technocracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T20:07:38-07:00","id":155402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/148021-hunters-are-nutcases?p=155324#post155324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In large part, it comes courtesy of Mage - quite literally, in fact. Yi the Archer was apparently a Mage (one version, anyway), and the equipment that SF0 uses is produced by the Technocracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh, the Technocracy, how I love thee. Perfect for inducing terror in players.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, what is that? You guys are badasses? No one can stop your rampage... oh no, look, its five hitmarks with primium armor. Awww, damn. Sucks to be you.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1604-oliver-the-bold","name":"Oliver the Bold","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T02:46:37-07:00","id":155570,"title":"","content":"I have Task Force: Valkyrie as the boogeyman in case my players start doing stupid things. Technocracy is the last option.<br /> <br /> Though this TF: V is slightly modified for my uses, as they recruit few supernaturals of their own, brainwa- taught by American citizens.<br /> <br /> Despite rumors, it is not manipulated by vampires. It is manipulated by wraiths, namely the wraith of Abraham Lincoln who got assassinated by unknown supernatural as according to backstory of the task force and along with his other ghostly allies, including other dead Presidents, he provides vital support to the operation.<br /> <br /> PS. When TZIMISCE awakens, it will be giant golems of Washington, Lincoln, Jefferson and Roosevelt, straight out of Mount Rushmore and empowered by the souls of whom they portrait, who shall go Liberty Prime on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":2918,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","user":"Kat","date":". 06-01-2014, 05:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T05:42:02-07:00","id":156412,"title":"","content":"I think I need to read Vigil, because it sounds a lot more like what I always expected of H:tR.<br /> <br /> <br /> Oliver the Bold said it well. Hunters who had true sight and were immune to supernatural powers would have felt much more &quot;anti-monster&quot; to me. As if their very existence was an anchor-point for mundane reality. And being immune to supernatural powers (to any degree) is almost more powerful than having them yourself.<br /> <br /> Since I am no Hunter expert, is this feasible (or preferably common) in either version?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T07:00:41-07:00","id":156463,"title":"","content":"HtR hunters are partially immune to monster powers when they spend Convinction; the only powers that work are of the &quot;I beat him until he dies&quot; variety. Without spending Conviction they're just normal people, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/426-big-brother","name":"Big Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar426_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T11:17:14-07:00","id":156752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Big Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/148021-hunters-are-nutcases?p=156463#post156463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">HtR hunters are partially immune to monster powers when they spend Convinction; the only powers that work are of the &quot;I beat him until he dies&quot; variety. Without spending Conviction they're just normal people, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but they have to spend it. What I was referring to was them simply having <i>innate </i>immunity offered by become Hunters. So it couldn't be something they could just turn off or ignore. Their view of the world had changed and would remain so, forever more. All that without the ability to summon flaming swords, throw bolts of lightning, summon the fog of death, imprison people with your mind, or reveal the secret world to others. You might learn Numina or Sorcery, but mostly you would have to rely on your wits. Also, it would make it much more challenging to protect others. As it stands the HtR Edges vary from completely useless to batshit powerful, pretty wildly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1604-oliver-the-bold","name":"Oliver the Bold","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T17:56:04-07:00","id":157146,"title":"","content":"Personally, I prefer the Bystander rules from <b>Hunter Player\u2019s Guide</b> to the full-blown Conviction-and-Edges system of <b>HtR</b>: no Creeds, no Edges; Conviction as a measure of how much staying power you have left; the Virtues of Courage, Reason, and Self-Control as bulwarks against degeneration of what\u2019s left of your Conviction; and what \u201cpowers\u201d they have take the form of supernatural Merits that serve as imperfect versions of native Imbued powers: perceptive Merits such as Supernatural Affinity, The Word, Penetrate Illusion, or the Sight; and protective Merits such as Cannot Become a Monster, Resistant to Supernatural Fear, or Resistant to Mind Control. (They also have an ability to recognize others of their kind \u2014 described as picking up on tell-tale body language etc. rather than a supernatural power \u2014 and to spend Willpower to shake off supernatural fear and mind control.)<br /> <br /> Beyond that and the \u201cabbreviated monsters\u201d featured in the various Enemy Books, I really don\u2019t have much use for the HtR line. While HtV is a cool game, I\u2019d suggest giving Bystanders a try first. Possibly mixed in with <b>Hunters Hunted 2</b>. Just disregard the flavor text that describes them as \u201cfailed Imbued\u201d, and play them as the <i>only</i> \u201cImbued\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 06-02-2014, 10:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T23:52:37-07:00","id":157566,"title":"","content":"Idle note: You know what the big supernatural TV series was when HtR came out? Buffy the Vampire Slayer.<br /> <br /> Reckoning is WW's take on a Buffy game, seen through the lens of a major splat in the cWOD. Ordinary person gets chosen to take on the supernatural beasties of the night, enhanced to be just a bit beyond normal human, unable to ignore the supernatural around them, torn between their ordinary life and their hunting life. Metaphysically, they're set apart, but the way they see the world is still grounded in everyday life.<br /> <br /> Hell, the girl on the cover of the Hunter Player's Guide is basically Buffy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T05:30:02-07:00","id":157740,"title":"","content":"Those Bystander rules are something I need to look into. Maybe I am old fashioned, but I always just used variations of &quot;True Faith&quot; for my hunters; not always faith in God but sometimes just faith in humanity to overcome the monsters - same mechanics different fluff. The rules you outline though sound like they <b>could</b> actually add something new and interesting, as opposed to &quot;the Imbued&quot; which most mages would see as marauders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T07:08:01-07:00","id":157797,"title":"","content":"My inclination would be to go the other way around: the traditional True Faith system simply doesn\u2019t have enough crunch for my taste; so I\u2019d rather reskin HtR\u2019s Imbued as \u201cthe Faithful\u201d. Conviction keeps the same name, but represents religious devotion; Virtues remain the same, except with broader definitions that relate to more things than just how you relate to monsters; and Edges become Miracles. Some minor tweaks involving how Edges work might be in order (such as allowing for Virtues and Edges to be lost, or allowing temporary access to Edges you lack in appropriate situations), but mostly, the system works for this as written. <br /> <br /> The Messengers don\u2019t Imbue just anyone; they restrict their blessings to the faithful. That is, religious devotion comes first, and then gets enhanced by the Messengers. (Of course, I also don\u2019t generally mess with the \u201cend times\u201d metaplot; so the notion that the Messengers are running around Imbuing random mortals as a last-ditch effort to stave off the end of the world doesn\u2019t work for me.) It\u2019s worth noting that the english translation for \u201cangel\u201d is \u201cmessenger\u201d, and that terms such as \u201cherald\u201d and \u201cminister\u201d are also suitable descriptions of what angels do. It\u2019s also worth noting that HtR\u2019s \u201cDark Ages\u201d counterpart was <b>Dark Ages: Inquisitor</b>. <br /> <br /> I still wouldn\u2019t associate Bystanders with the Imbued: in my games, the origin of Bystanders (who don\u2019t even have a collective name) is a mystery, and is largely unrelated to the Messengers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T20:26:02-07:00","id":158619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/148021-hunters-are-nutcases?p=157797#post157797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My inclination would be to go the other way around: the traditional True Faith system simply doesn\u2019t have enough crunch for my taste; so I\u2019d rather reskin HtR\u2019s Imbued as \u201cthe Faithful\u201d. Conviction keeps the same name, but represents religious devotion; Virtues remain the same, except with broader definitions that relate to more things than just how you relate to monsters; and Edges become Miracles. Some minor tweaks involving how Edges work might be in order (such as allowing for Virtues and Edges to be lost, or allowing temporary access to Edges you lack in appropriate situations), but mostly, the system works for this as written.<br /> <br /> The Messengers don\u2019t Imbue just anyone; they restrict their blessings to the faithful. That is, religious devotion comes first, and then gets enhanced by the Messengers. (Of course, I also don\u2019t generally mess with the \u201cend times\u201d metaplot; so the notion that the Messengers are running around Imbuing random mortals as a last-ditch effort to stave off the end of the world doesn\u2019t work for me.) It\u2019s worth noting that the english translation for \u201cangel\u201d is \u201cmessenger\u201d, and that terms such as \u201cherald\u201d and \u201cminister\u201d are also suitable descriptions of what angels do. I<u>t\u2019s also worth noting that HtR\u2019s \u201cDark Ages\u201d counterpart was <b>Dark Ages: Inquisitor</b>.</u><br /> <br /> I still wouldn\u2019t associate Bystanders with the Imbued: in my games, the origin of Bystanders (who don\u2019t even have a collective name) is a mystery, and is largely unrelated to the Messengers.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a contrast, Changeling's counterpart was Dark Ages: Fae, which was about a somewhat similar but ultimately different order of being compared to the modern &quot;equivalent&quot;. I think that Inquisitor got paired up with Hunter for even thinner reasons, mostly having to do with Reckoning being tied so closely to the modern metaplot and thus leaving no Imbued proper as possible characters eight centuries in the past. So they just went with Vatican Ninja instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T21:06:55-07:00","id":158672,"title":"","content":"Well\u2026 kinda sorta. As I mentioned just before the part you underlined, there are a <i>lot</i> of parallels between the benefactors of the Imbued and the Judeo-Christian Heavenly Host. Between that and the way the Dark Ages Inquisition echoes much of <b>Hunter: the Reckoning</b>\u2019s mechanics (deliberately so); <i>and</i> the fact that the terminology for Hunter is pretty close to what you\u2019d expect of \u201cempowered to fight the forces of evil by the agents of good\u201d, <i>plus</i> the Player Guide\u2019s suggestion under its discussion about True Faith that the player who wants a devoutly religious character with supernatural powers should consider portraying his Edges as Divine Intervention, and I think there are plenty of grounds for thinking of Imbuements as being conceptually related to True Faith <i>at the very least</i>, and potentially as a viable basis for a game mechanical replacement for True Faith.<br /> <br /> If you\u2019re not going to be playing in a \u201cFinal Nights\u201d scenario, such a recasting of HtR as a game about the Faithful (with a capital \u201cF\u201d) is pretty much the only way that something resembling the Imbued could have any place at all in the setting.<br /> <br /> Mind you, some tweaking would be in order; for a setup where \u201cImbued\u201d becomes \u201cBlessed\u201d, I\u2019d want to incorporate some elements of <b>Dark Ages: Inquisitor</b> as well, such as something to the effect of Piety and the way it interacts with Conviction.<br /> <br /> I would also say that they didn\u2019t <i>have to</i> do a Dark Ages counterpart for <b>Hunter</b>. They didn\u2019t do one for <b>Wraith</b> or <b>Mummy</b> (though I wish they had gotten around to the former; the Dark Ages were interesting times in the Shadowlands). That they chose to do so, <i>and</i> chose to use the Medieval Inquisition as its basis, has some interesting implications. <br /> <br /> BTW: <b>Dark Ages: Fae</b> was radically different from <b>Changeling: the Dreaming</b> in part because the Dark Ages timeframe was set before the time of the Sundering as defined in <b>Changeling</b>. Sure, they took full advantage of that fact to develop what many consider to be what <b>Changeling</b> <i>should have been</i>; but they didn\u2019t just up and decide to do things differently just for the sake of doing things differently. It\u2019s a different game; but it\u2019s one that\u2019s nevertheless rooted in <b>Changeling</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 06-04-2014, 01:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T00:01:12-07:00","id":158766,"title":"","content":"For some reason, I had it in my head that Hunters were a take on serial killers. Viewed externally, that's what they would seem like. The Hunter Glyphs are reminiscent of the Zodiac Killer. The voices of the Messengers are reminiscent of the David Berkowitz, the Son of Sam.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/260-chase-variant","name":"Chase Variant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar260_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T02:28:35-07:00","id":158852,"title":"","content":"I can agree with Chase on that point, as they would very easily be qualified as serial killers by the government/police. I see it similar to Sam &amp; Dean from Supernatural in that respect, sure they are killing off nasty things that prey on humanity but the police have no clue that they are doing anything but killing people. Hunters can claim that voices from God told them X person was evil and had to die, but that's just going to add fuel to the fire and make it even more likely they'll be put away for a long time. Hunter-net would just look like a hangout of delusional paranoid serial killers sharing tips, tricks, and info and the glyphs just an odd form of tagging.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I'm immortal, I've been right so far&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/301-bwchism","name":"bwchism","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar301_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T03:06:48-07:00","id":158867,"title":"","content":"I have trouble picturing Innocents, Defenders, Martyrs, or Visionaries as serial killers. Redeemers, Judges, and Avengers, maybe; Waywards, definitely; and Hermits are a different brand of crazy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T08:00:47-07:00","id":159046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/148021-hunters-are-nutcases?p=148426#post148426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> There's plenty enough &quot;you just don't know&quot; just in being out of the loop on who's empowering you and why, or what you're capable of. We don't need to turn <i>They Live</i> with things that go bump in the night into <i>Frailty</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sadly that was the.. thing. You were supposed to descend into the average chat room (before the grouping happened that social media reopened) And &quot;you are going crazy but can't be sure&quot; especially as the ultimate weapon in oWoD was psychic powers that cleared away objective reality. You couldn't see or prove anything and STs were encouraged to screw with you so you couldn't use logic and your hunting made you a crazy zealotous monster...unless you slept with a monster and woke up you were suppose to really not personally invest as much.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1498-darmani","name":"Darmani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1498_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T10:02:55-07:00","id":159165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darmani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/148021-hunters-are-nutcases?p=159046#post159046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sadly that was the.. thing. You were supposed to descend into the average chat room (before the grouping happened that social media reopened) And &quot;you are going crazy but can't be sure&quot; especially as the ultimate weapon in oWoD was psychic powers that cleared away objective reality. You couldn't see or prove anything and STs were encouraged to screw with you so you couldn't use logic and your hunting made you a crazy zealotous monster...unless you slept with a monster and woke up you were suppose to really not personally invest as much.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Which leads me to an interesting idea...<br /> <br /> Couldn't a Mage with enough hunter lore just create his own hunters? I mean... giving them &quot;sight&quot; and talking to them in their mind are very easy tricks. Granting them (sometimes) amazing powers wouldn't be too difficult.<br /> <br /> Having your very own murderous lunatic on a leash who believes your very word is the word of God? Priceless.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> (This was <i>partially</i> tongue in cheek)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T12:50:14-07:00","id":159291,"title":"","content":"Unless you are the Exemplar of Prime, gonna have some difficulties with that SixFootChicken. The least of which is Paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1604-oliver-the-bold","name":"Oliver the Bold","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T13:47:14-07:00","id":159335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oliver the Bold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/148021-hunters-are-nutcases?p=159291#post159291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless you are the Exemplar of Prime, gonna have some difficulties with that SixFootChicken. The least of which is Paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehh, maybe / maybe not. The devil is in the details.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T20:34:51-07:00","id":159692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SixFootChicken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/148021-hunters-are-nutcases?p=159165#post159165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which leads me to an interesting idea...<br /> <br /> Couldn't a Mage with enough hunter lore just create his own hunters? I mean... giving them &quot;sight&quot; and talking to them in their mind are very easy tricks. Granting them (sometimes) amazing powers wouldn't be too difficult.<br /> <br /> Having your very own murderous lunatic on a leash who believes your very word is the word of God? Priceless.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> (This was <i>partially</i> tongue in cheek)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Those would probably come out looking like the Mockery Breeds from Book of the Wyrm W20, only with Imbued mechanics instead of Werewolf ones, and the Mage is likely to end up suffering some dramatic change in existential status for it, almost overwhelmingly likely to the negative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T05:20:07-07:00","id":159912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/148021-hunters-are-nutcases?p=159692#post159692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Those would probably come out looking like the Mockery Breeds from Book of the Wyrm W20, only with Imbued mechanics instead of Werewolf ones, and the Mage is likely to end up suffering some dramatic change in existential status for it, almost overwhelmingly likely to the negative.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't seen that yet, I will check it out just for shits and giggles.<br /> <br /> And yes, this would absolutely have horrible long term consequences for the mage... but that's part of the fun of hubris!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T07:37:29-07:00","id":164822,"title":"","content":"I fail to be surprised when any post about <b>Reckoning</b> turns into a discussion about how <b>Vigil </b>is a better game even though the latter wasn't even mentioned in the OP. We've been hearing that <b>Reckoning </b>sucks by the majority of the community's standards since it was released in late '99. Let's let the now skelefied horse be, hmm? Some people love it. Most seem to hate it. I am one of the former having <b>Reckoning </b>be the game I chose to buy from among the WoD core books available at the time. It wasn't entirely what I expected from the marketing, but it was definitely all kinds of awesome. It let me play a human in a game line where a human was usually just food or a plaything.<br /> <br /> This brings me to the next point that wasn't part of the OP. Are the Imbued human? I think so. However, &quot;We're not a blip on our own monster radar!&quot; is shaky reasoning at best. I believe the question was deliberately left open for debate and we may never have a definitive answer.<br /> <br /> Now to the actual question at hand: Yes, they are all nutty. Every last one of them. By average human thinking standards, they are aberrant and strange in their thinking and worldview. It doesn't matter that the majority of the human race is dead wrong about the existence of monsters and the Hunters are right. Because they are in the minority compared to the consensus, they are insane to think something is fundamentally different from what the vast majority of humanity believes.<br /> <br /> I was able to play a Defender for a few sessions that didn't immediately take out all the &quot;threats&quot; he saw (this is how his Sight operated) because there were just so many of them and he needed to pick his fights. Also, not all of these creatures were posing immediate danger to his charge (the entire female student population past, present, and future of the college he attended), or at least as near as he could tell. It was a mixed game, so he had to play nice and I was easily able to find legitimate story reasons to do so.<br /> <br /> Let me clarify one point in closing: I love <b>Vigil</b>. It delivered on many things I was hoping <b>Reckoning </b>would be. I am very fond of <b>Reckoning</b> because I grew to appreciate what it was instead of what I thought it should have been. <b>Vigil </b>is a different sort of beast and a beautiful one at that. I would gladly play either one. I just am pretty tired of all the hate thrown at my favorite CWoD game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T13:57:04-07:00","id":165133,"title":"","content":"Agreed with everything you just said \u2014 although I do find it interesting that your chosen \u201cdefense\u201d for HtR (which, I understand, wasn\u2019t intended as a defense) is essentially \u201cthey\u2019re not <i>all</i> bad.\u201d I\u2019m not so much in the camp of \u201c<b>Vigil</b> is better than <b>Reckoning</b>\u201d as \u201cthe Year of the Hunter and related books were more to my liking than <b>Reckoning</b> was\u201d. <br /> <br /> But I <i>do</i> agree that <b>Reckoning</b> had its good points, not the least of which was that the Imbued had at least some protection against the \u201cI win\u201d buttons that had been handed out to so many monsters by that point (Delirium, the Mists, etc.): lacking any powers of his own, the only chance a human has against monsters is to keep his wits about him; so passive \u201cmental tampering\u201d effects are especially damaging as they undermine the hunter\u2019s only means of survival. <br /> <br /> But the OP hit upon my single biggest issue with the Imbued: no matter how much you might say that they\u2019re \u201cstill human\u201d, they have powers that are not natural to humanity, and they don\u2019t see the world the way normal humans do (<i>literally</i> even, due to the Sight). To one extent or another, every last one of them is nuts; and they\u2019re no more human than mages are (a point that I\u2019m grateful that <b>Spellbound</b> brought up). That\u2019s why my perspective on <b>Reckoning</b> is that it\u2019s a good line to mine for ideas; but it\u2019s <i>not</i> a game I have any interest in playing anywhere close to as-is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T14:14:48-07:00","id":165146,"title":"","content":"I wasn't trying to defend anything as much as I was trying to express my exasperation in a civil manner. I would probably do the same for the other CWoD game lines when someone started beating on them with the same &quot;NWoD version is better!&quot; argument in a thread that has nothing to do with a comparison between the C and N lines. For the love of Richard &quot;Deadguy&quot; Dansky we know <b>Time of Judgement </b>happened. We know NWoD was launched. We are not trying to hand wave all the good work that is NWoD away. We enjoy the CWoD games that we enjoy. Leave it at that.<br /> <br /> <b>Year of the Hunter</b> was darn awesome as far as I'm concerned, too. I think the thing that causes me to like the Imbued more is the possibility that they could be Divinely Imbued. I tend to play Knights in Shining Armor every chance I get. Plus, I'm always that one guy that picks human as my race in games. To me, Imbued are the most human (while still nutty) I can get in the CWoD and not automatically be screwed by all the &quot;Win&quot; buttons the monsters get. Mages are better able to maintain their humanity, but there is way too much potential for them to believe they are superior.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T15:06:59-07:00","id":165249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belkra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/148021-hunters-are-nutcases?p=165146#post165146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn't trying to defend anything as much as I was trying to express my exasperation in a civil manner. I would probably do the same for the other CWoD game lines when someone started beating on them with the same &quot;NWoD version is better!&quot; argument in a thread that has nothing to do with a comparison between the C and N lines. For the love of Richard &quot;Deadguy&quot; Dansky we know <b>Time of Judgement </b>happened. We know NWoD was launched. We are not trying to hand wave all the good work that is NWoD away. We enjoy the CWoD games that we enjoy. Leave it at that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I fully sympathize with this, and have made my own arguments that N vs. C should be thought of in terms of personal preferences rather than objective \u201cX is better than Y\u201d comparisons, if they\u2019re to be compared at all. This is especially true now that the first three nWoD gamelines are getting overhauls designed in part to distinguish them further from their oWoD counterparts. That said, I\u2019m quite happy that Time of Judgment has <i>un</i>happened. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belkra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/148021-hunters-are-nutcases?p=165146#post165146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Year of the Hunter</b> was darn awesome as far as I'm concerned, too. I think the thing that causes me to like the Imbued more is the possibility that they could be Divinely Imbued. I tend to play Knights in Shining Armor every chance I get. Plus, I'm always that one guy that picks human as my race in games. To me, Imbued are the most human (while still nutty) I can get in the CWoD and not automatically be screwed by all the &quot;Win&quot; buttons the monsters get. Mages are better able to maintain their humanity, but there is way too much potential for them to believe they are superior.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah; I know what you mean. These are the reasons why I like to graft <b>Reckoning</b>\u2019s Bystander rules and their less blatantly supernatural defenses against supernatural \u201cI win\u201d buttons onto <b>Hunters Hunted</b>/<b>Year of the Hunter</b>-style hunters, and prefer to hack <b>Reckoning</b> into more of a \u201cModern Ages: Inquisitor\u201d type replacement for True Faith. As I said, I have little interest in playing <b>Reckoning</b> as written; but it has some useful things that can be mined for use in something that I <i>would</i> be willing to play. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T15:53:33-07:00","id":165315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belkra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/148021-hunters-are-nutcases?p=165146#post165146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...the same &quot;NWoD version is better!&quot; argument in a thread that has nothing to do with a comparison between the C and N lines...</div> </div> </div> </div>This. Right here. This.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/426-big-brother","name":"Big Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar426_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}